      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pressure to keep producing is relentless, and that feeling of needing to \"break\" is a desperate call for release. Reclaiming yourself after feeling hollowed out is a slow, messy process, but it's not guaranteed to be a clean break. If the system demands everything, perhaps the most radical act is finding a way to make your own silence louder than its demands.",
